    <!--
        Default Color Palette

        Specifies which color palette to use by default.
        Must match one of the palette names defined in "Color Palettes" below,
        or use "None" for no colorization.

        Available palettes: Spectrum, Christmas, Halloween, Pride, Valentine, Easter,
        USA, Ocean, Sunset, Forest, Monochrome, Neon

        Default: "Spectrum"
    -->
    <key>Color Palette</key>
    <string>Spectrum</string>

    <!--
        Color Palettes

        Defines the available color palettes for logo coloring.

        Format:
        - Each palette is an array of color definitions
        - Each color definition must have a "Color Space" key ("RGB" or "HSV")
        - For RGB: Red, Green, Blue, Alpha (0.0-1.0)
        - For HSV: Hue (0-360 degrees), Saturation, Value, Alpha (0.0-1.0)
        - Values can be discrete (e.g., <real>0.5</real>) or ranges (e.g., <string>0.13...0.87</string>)

        Special palette:
        - "None": No colorization (do not define in this file)

        To add a new palette:
        1. Choose a descriptive name
        2. Define an array of color dictionaries
        3. Each color must have "Color Space" and component keys
        4. Update the "Color Palette" key above if you want it as the default
    -->
